	(text "Generated from docs/ac30_PS.pdf (SWTPC AC-30 Audio Cassette Power Supply Schematic).\nBuilt as an EXTERNAL unit: these parts have no footprints and are not on the PC board. Wire the\nsix outputs (+5V, GND, +13V, -13V, +7.5V, -7.5V) to the board's power pads TP1-TP6.\nTranscription notes / corrections:\n - The drawing joins the IC16 GND / C23-C25 return line to the bridge's negative corner (-13 V)\n   through two crossings. That would put the 7805's ground at -13 V, so IC16 GND is taken as GND.\n - T1's two 120 V primaries are drawn in parallel (120 VAC); drawn here as one primary. The\n   18 VAC secondary is centre-tapped, tap to GND: the bridge gives +13 V (C21) and -13 V (C22).\n - D14-D17 numbering within the bridge is not shown on the drawing; assigned here.\n - S6 is an SPDT toggle (BOM) used as an on/off switch; one throw is unused.\n - IC15 (1488) supply pins are not drawn on the switching schematic; taken as +/-13 V, the only\n   load for those outputs. IC4 (4558) uses +/-7.5 V (assembly manual)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0c562ef8-8fe0-5091-bb3e-390ed69a74fa")
	)
	(text "Power supply (external): 120 VAC -> T1 -> bridge D14-D17 -> +/-13 V, zeners +/-7.5 V, 7805 +5 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 60 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4fee44de-a81e-5bac-a191-41e6c4681e90")
	)
